- **Specific Code Behavior Causing Vulnerability:** The code reads 9 bytes from the input stream without checking if there are at least 9 bytes available. This can lead to an out-of-bounds read, potentially allowing an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service.
- **Solution Behavior:** Check if there are at least 9 bytes remaining in the input stream before attempting to read them. This ensures that the function only reads data from the input stream when there is enough data available, preventing the out-of-bounds read from occurring.

